model law04
  tally 1
  on 2026-10-25
  start 2022-01-01
  end 2023-12-31
  note "Probe LAW-04: a rate cut enacted in July for the whole year. The monthly advances keep their booked amounts (arrears none); the return reads what was booked and settles the difference on its own day."
  note "The card's facts and its earlier law are stipulations, known from start (L 4.5). The act is a later dated document: published in July 2022, no day given."

source card "Probe card LAW-04 (tmp/cases/probes/law/LAW-04.md): story, rules 1-2 and question"

index mo = month 2022-01..2022-12

index yr = year 2022..2022

place ania: account DUK

place tax_office: outside DUK

input adv_day: int

input adv_rate: num question "What advance rate applies to this month's pay?"

input filed[y in yr]: date question "On what day is the return for this year filed?"

input monthly: money DUK question "What does Ania earn a month?"

input year_rate[y in yr]: num question "What rate does the year's law set for this year's income?"

def adv_amt[m in mo]: money DUK
  note "the advance on the month's pay at the month's rate. The card states no rounding; every advance is a whole number of minor units, so the mode changes nothing"
  rule base v card_payroll = round(adv_rate * monthly, 0.01, half-up)

def due[y in yr]: money DUK
  note "rule 1: the year's law applied to the year's income; exact here, so the mode changes nothing"
  rule base v card_return = round(year_rate[y] * income[y], 0.01, half-up)

def income[y in yr]: money DUK = sum(m in mo where year_of(m) = y: monthly)

def withheld[y in yr]: money DUK
  note "rule 1: what was withheld is credited: the advances as booked, corrections included (L 5.13.3)"
  rule base v card_return = flows(advance, y)

pay advance[m in mo]
  from ania
  to tax_office
  amount adv_amt[m]
  on day_of(m, adv_day)
  for m

pay arrears_paid[y in yr]
  from ania
  to tax_office
  amount due[y] - withheld[y]
  on filed[y]
  for y
  when due[y] > withheld[y]

pay refund[y in yr]
  from tax_office
  to ania
  amount withheld[y] - due[y]
  on filed[y]
  for y
  when withheld[y] > due[y]

ask months_kept: flows(advance[m], m) for m in mo

ask settlement: withheld[2022], due[2022], flows(refund, 2023-04-30), flows(arrears_paid, 2023), flows(ania, 2023-04-30)

version card_facts
  cite card
  known 2022-01-01
  adv_day = 28 assumed "the card gives no day for the monthly advances; a pay needs a date (L 5.9), so the 28th stands for it; no figure asked depends on the day"
  filed[2022] = 2023-04-30 "story: she files her return on 30 April 2023"
  monthly = 8000 "story: Ania earns 8 000.00 DUK a month in 2022"

version card_payroll
  cite card
  known 2022-01-01
  note "story: her advances were 17 % to June and 12 % from July"
  adv_rate = 0.17 governs 2022-01..2022-06 "story: 17 % to June"
  adv_rate = 0.12 governs 2022-07.. "story: 12 % from July"

version card_return
  cite card
  known 2022-01-01
  note "rules 1-2: no items; the return's rules point at it"

version card_act
  cite card
  governs 2022
  known 2022-07-31
  arrears none for advance
  note "the act published in July 2022; the card gives no day, so known takes the latest it can be, 31 July (L 4.5, Knowledge)"
  note "rule 2: a change covering a closed period is booked on the day it is settled, never by rewriting past months: no back pay on the advances; the return settles it"
  adv_rate = 0.12 governs 2022-01..2022-06 "story: the act cuts the rate to 12 % for the whole of 2022 (July to December were 12 % already)"
  year_rate[2022] = 0.12 "story: 12 % for the whole of 2022, which the return applies (rule 1)"
